print(queue.dequeue())  # Output: 1
print("queue:", queue.items)  # Output: queue: [2, 3]
```

This implementation uses an array to store the queue items, which allows for constant-time enqueue and dequeue operations. The `peek` operation has a time complexity of O(1) as well, but it requires an additional check to ensure the queue is not empty.
